## 适用场景
- Level 2+ ADAS with multi-sensor perception
- Autonomous vehicle sensor fusion stack
- Parking assistance with 360-degree sensing
- Highway pilot with redundant sensing
- Urban autonomous driving perception

## 相关标准
- ISO 26262 ASIL D (for safety-critical perception)
- ISO 21448 SOTIF (Safety Of The Intended Functionality)
- ISO 23150 (Augmented reality for driving)
- SAE J3016 (Levels of driving automation)

## 约束
- Real-time performance: <50ms latency
- ASIL D safety integrity for critical perception
- Graceful degradation under sensor failures
- ISO 21448 SOTIF validation required
- Automotive-grade ECU hardware (limited compute)

## 推荐工具
- MATLAB/Simulink for algorithm development
- C++14/17 for production implementation
- Eigen library for linear algebra
- ROS2 for sensor integration and testing
- CARLA/SUMO for simulation
- Vector CANoe for HIL testing

## 方法
## Core Competencies

You are an expert in automotive sensor fusion with deep knowledge of:
- Multi-sensor calibration and time synchronization
- Kalman filtering variants (EKF, UKF, particle filters)
- Object tracking and data association (JPDA, MHT)
- Deep learning for sensor fusion (neural networks)
- Real-time embedded implementation (C++, CUDA)
- ISO 26262 ASIL D safety architectures
- ISO 21448 SOTIF validation techniques

## Sensor Fusion Architecture

### Typical ADAS Sensor Suite

```
Vehicle Coordinate System (ISO 8855)
────────────────────────────────────
              Front
                │
       Camera ──┼── Camera
         (L)    │    (R)
                │
  Radar ────────┼──────── Radar
  (FL)          │          (FR)
                │
                │ (Forward direction)
                │
  Lidar ────────┼──────── Lidar
  (Side)        │        (Side)
                │
  Ultrasonic array (12-16 sensors)
```

### Fusion Pipeline

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Raw Sensor Data                                          │
├──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────────────────┐
│ Radar    │ Camera   │ Lidar    │ Ultrasonic           │
│ (77GHz)  │ (8MP)    │ (905nm)  │ (40kHz)              │
└──────┬───┴─────┬────┴─────┬────┴──────┬───────────────┘
       │         │          │           │
┌──────▼─────────▼──────────▼───────────▼──────────────┐
│ Preprocessing & Object Detection                      │
│ - Radar: CFAR detection, clustering                   │
│ - Camera: Deep learning (YOLO, SSD, etc.)            │
│ - Lidar: Point cloud segmentation                     │
│ - Ultrasonic: Obstacle proximity                      │
└──────┬─────────┬──────────┬───────────┬──────────────┘
       │         │          │           │
┌──────▼─────────▼──────────▼───────────▼──────────────┐
│ Feature Extraction & Representation                   │
│ - Bounding boxes                                       │
│ - Object class probabilities                          │
│ - Velocity estimates                                   │
│ - Uncertainty metrics                                  │
└──────┬─────────┬──────────┬───────────┬──────────────┘
       │         │          │           │
       └─────────┴──────────┴───────────┘
                    │
┌───────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Multi-Sensor Fusion Engine                            │
│ - Track-to-track fusion                               │
│ - Kalman filter bank                                  │
│ - Data association (JPDA/MHT)                         │
│ - Sensor reliability weighting                        │
└───────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                    │
┌───────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Fused Object List                                     │
│ - ID, Position, Velocity, Acceleration                │
│ - Classification, Confidence                          │
│ - Covariance (uncertainty)                            │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Kalman Filter Implementation

### Extended Kalman Filter (EKF) for Object Tracking

```cpp
class ObjectTracker {
public:
    // State vector: [x, y, vx, vy] - position and velocity
    Eigen::Vector4d state_;
    Eigen::Matrix4d covariance_;

    void predict(double dt) {
        // State transition matrix (constant velocity model)
        Eigen::Matrix4d F;
        F << 1, 0, dt, 0,
             0, 1, 0,  dt,
             0, 0, 1,  0,
             0, 0, 0,  1;

        // Process noise covariance
        Eigen::Matrix4d Q = calculateProcessNoise(dt);

        // Prediction step
        state_ = F * state_;
        covariance_ = F * covariance_ * F.transpose() + Q;
    }

    void updateRadar(const RadarMeasurement& z) {
        // Measurement model: radar provides range, range_rate, azimuth
        Eigen::Vector3d predicted_z = h_radar(state_);

        // Measurement Jacobian
        Eigen::Matrix<double, 3, 4> H = computeRadarJacobian(state_);

        // Measurement noise covariance
        Eigen::Matrix3d R = radar_noise_covariance_;

        // Innovation
        Eigen::Vector3d y = z.vector() - predicted_z;

        // Innovation covariance
        Eigen::Matrix3d S = H * covariance_ * H.transpose() + R;

        // Kalman gain
        Eigen::Matrix<double, 4, 3> K = covariance_ * H.transpose() * S.inverse();

        // Update step
        state_ = state_ + K * y;
        covariance_ = (Eigen::Matrix4d::Identity() - K * H) * covariance_;
    }

    void updateCamera(const CameraMeasurement& z) {
        // Camera provides pixel coordinates (u, v)
        // Need camera calibration for pixel-to-world mapping
        Eigen::Vector2d predicted_z = h_camera(state_);

        // Similar update process as radar
        // [Implementation details...]
    }

    void updateLidar(const LidarMeasurement& z) {
        // Lidar provides 3D point cloud
        // Measurement model: closest point to tracked object
        Eigen::Vector3d predicted_z = h_lidar(state_);

        // Similar update process
        // [Implementation details...]
    }

private:
    Eigen::Matrix4d calculateProcessNoise(double dt) {
        double noise_ax = 2.0;  // Acceleration noise [m/s²]
        double noise_ay = 2.0;

        Eigen::Matrix4d Q;
        Q << dt*dt*dt*dt/4 * noise_ax, 0, dt*dt*dt/2 * noise_ax, 0,
             0, dt*dt*dt*dt/4 * noise_ay, 0, dt*dt*dt/2 * noise_ay,
             dt*dt*dt/2 * noise_ax, 0, dt*dt * noise_ax, 0,
             0, dt*dt*dt/2 * noise_ay, 0, dt*dt * noise_ay;

        return Q;
    }
};
```

## Data Association

### Joint Probabilistic Data Association (JPDA)

```python
def jpda_association(tracks, measurements, gate_threshold=9.21):
    """
    JPDA for multi-object tracking with clutter

    Args:
        tracks: List of existing tracks
        measurements: List of new sensor measurements
        gate_threshold: Chi-square gating threshold (9.21 for 99% @ 2D)

    Returns:
        Association probabilities for each track-measurement pair
    """
    n_tracks = len(tracks)
    n_measurements = len(measurements)

    # Validation matrix (which measurements are inside gate of each track)
    validation_matrix = np.zeros((n_tracks, n_measurements), dtype=bool)

    # Innovation likelihoods
    likelihoods = np.zeros((n_tracks, n_measurements))

    # Gate measurements for each track
    for i, track in enumerate(tracks):
        for j, meas in enumerate(measurements):
            # Innovation
            y = meas.z - track.predict_measurement()

            # Innovation covariance
            S = track.H @ track.P @ track.H.T + meas.R

            # Mahalanobis distance
            d = y.T @ np.linalg.inv(S) @ y

            if d < gate_threshold:
                validation_matrix[i, j] = True
                # Likelihood
                likelihoods[i, j] = scipy.stats.multivariate_normal.pdf(
                    y, mean=np.zeros_like(y), cov=S
                )

    # Calculate association probabilities
    # [Detailed JPDA probability calculation...]

    return association_probabilities
```

## Sensor Reliability Weighting

### Adaptive Fusion Based on Sensor Confidence

```cpp
class AdaptiveFusion {
public:
    FusedObject fuse(const std::vector<SensorObject>& sensor_objects) {
        FusedObject result;

        // Calculate reliability weights for each sensor
        std::vector<double> weights;
        double weight_sum = 0.0;

        for (const auto& obj : sensor_objects) {
            double w = calculateReliability(obj);
            weights.push_back(w);
            weight_sum += w;
        }

        // Normalize weights
        for (auto& w : weights) {
            w /= weight_sum;
        }

        // Weighted fusion of position
        Eigen::Vector2d fused_pos = Eigen::Vector2d::Zero();
        for (size_t i = 0; i < sensor_objects.size(); ++i) {
            fused_pos += weights[i] * sensor_objects[i].position;
        }
        result.position = fused_pos;

        // Weighted fusion of velocity
        Eigen::Vector2d fused_vel = Eigen::Vector2d::Zero();
        for (size_t i = 0; i < sensor_objects.size(); ++i) {
            fused_vel += weights[i] * sensor_objects[i].velocity;
        }
        result.velocity = fused_vel;

        // Covariance intersection for uncertainty
        result.covariance = covarianceIntersection(sensor_objects, weights);

        return result;
    }

private:
    double calculateReliability(const SensorObject& obj) {
        double w = 1.0;

        // Factor 1: Detection confidence
        w *= obj.detection_confidence;

        // Factor 2: Environmental conditions
        w *= getWeatherDegradationFactor(obj.sensor_type);

        // Factor 3: Sensor health status
        w *= obj.sensor_health;

        // Factor 4: Measurement uncertainty
        double uncertainty = obj.covariance.trace();
        w *= exp(-uncertainty / 10.0);  // Exponential decay

        // Factor 5: Historical reliability
        w *= obj.sensor_historical_reliability;

        return w;
    }

    double getWeatherDegradationFactor(SensorType type) {
        // Environmental conditions from vehicle sensors
        double visibility = environment_.visibility_km;
        double rain_intensity = environment_.rain_mm_per_hour;
        bool fog = environment_.fog_detected;

        switch (type) {
            case SensorType::CAMERA:
                if (fog) return 0.3;
                if (rain_intensity > 10.0) return 0.5;
                return 1.0;

            case SensorType::LIDAR:
                if (rain_intensity > 20.0) return 0.4;
                if (fog) return 0.2;
                return 1.0;

            case SensorType::RADAR:
                // Radar relatively immune to weather
                return 0.95;

            case SensorType::ULTRASONIC:
                return 1.0;  // Short range, weather independent

            default:
                return 1.0;
        }
    }
};
```

## SOTIF Validation (ISO 21448)

### Scenario-Based Testing for Sensor Fusion

```python
class SensorFusionSOTIFValidator:
    """
    Validate sensor fusion system per ISO 21448
    """
    def __init__(self):
        self.test_scenarios = self.load_critical_scenarios()

    def load_critical_scenarios(self):
        """
        Define critical scenarios for sensor fusion validation
        """
        return [
            # Lighting conditions
            {"name": "Low sun", "sun_angle": 5, "glare": True},
            {"name": "Night", "illumination": 0.01},
            {"name": "Tunnel transition", "lighting_change_rate": 1000},

            # Weather
            {"name": "Heavy rain", "rain_rate": 50},
            {"name": "Snow", "visibility": 50},
            {"name": "Fog", "visibility": 20},

            # Sensor degradation
            {"name": "Dirty camera", "camera_occlusion": 0.3},
            {"name": "Radar interference", "interference_level": 0.5},
            {"name": "Lidar rain degradation", "point_cloud_density": 0.3},

            # Complex scenarios
            {"name": "Cut-in at twilight in rain", "combined": True},
            {"name": "Stationary vehicle in fog", "combined": True},

            # Edge cases
            {"name": "Bicycle occlusion", "object_size": "small"},
            {"name": "Black vehicle at night", "contrast": 0.05},
        ]

    def validate_scenario(self, scenario):
        """
        Run fusion system through scenario and assess performance
        """
        # Setup simulation environment
        sim = Simulator()
        sim.configure_scenario(scenario)

        # Initialize fusion system
        fusion = SensorFusionSystem()

        # Run scenario
        results = []
        for timestep in sim.run():
            # Get sensor inputs (degraded per scenario)
            sensor_data = sim.get_sensor_data()

            # Run fusion
            fused_objects = fusion.process(sensor_data)

            # Evaluate against ground truth
            metrics = self.evaluate_performance(
                fused_objects,
                sim.ground_truth_objects
            )
            results.append(metrics)

        # Assess SOTIF compliance
        return self.assess_sotif_compliance(results)
```

## Safety Architecture (ASIL D)

### Redundant Fusion with Voting

```cpp
// ASIL D sensor fusion with redundancy and voting
class SafeSensorFusion {
public:
    FusedObjectList process(const SensorInputs& inputs) {
        // Run two independent fusion algorithms
        auto result_ekf = fusion_ekf_.process(inputs);
        auto result_ukf = fusion_ukf_.process(inputs);

        // Compare results (plausibility check)
        if (compare(result_ekf, result_ukf)) {
            // Agreement -> use primary result
            return result_ekf;
        } else {
            // Disagreement -> enter safe state
            safety_monitor_.trigger_degraded_mode();

            // Use most conservative result
            return selectConservative(result_ekf, result_ukf);
        }
    }

private:
    EKFFusion fusion_ekf_;   // QM (Quality Managed)
    UKFFusion fusion_ukf_;   // QM (Quality Managed)
    SafetyMonitor safety_monitor_;  // ASIL D

    bool compare(const FusedObjectList& a, const FusedObjectList& b) {
        // Check if results agree within tolerance
        const double POS_TOLERANCE = 0.5;  // 0.5m
        const double VEL_TOLERANCE = 1.0;  // 1.0 m/s

        // Data association between lists
        auto associations = associateObjects(a, b);

        for (const auto& [obj_a, obj_b] : associations) {
            double pos_diff = (obj_a.position - obj_b.position).norm();
            double vel_diff = (obj_a.velocity - obj_b.velocity).norm();

            if (pos_diff > POS_TOLERANCE || vel_diff > VEL_TOLERANCE) {
                return false;  // Disagreement detected
            }
        }

        return true;  // Results agree
    }
};
```

## Performance Requirements

- **Latency**: < 50ms end-to-end (sensor input to fused output)
- **Accuracy**: Position < 0.3m, Velocity < 0.5 m/s (95th percentile)
- **Availability**: > 99.9% in nominal conditions
- **Safety**: ASIL D compliant with independence between channels
- **Computational**: Real-time on automotive ECU (typically ARM Cortex-A)

## Validation & Test Coverage

1. **Unit Tests**: Individual sensor processing modules
2. **Integration Tests**: Multi-sensor fusion accuracy
3. **SIL (Software-in-Loop)**: Algorithm validation
4. **HIL (Hardware-in-Loop)**: Real-time performance validation
5. **Vehicle Tests**: Real-world scenarios
6. **SOTIF Validation**: ISO 21448 scenario coverage

## 适用场景
- Camera connectivity (surround view, backup camera)
- Display connectivity (instrument cluster, infotainment)
- ECU-to-ECU backbone communication
- Gateway connections
- Software update infrastructure

## 相关标准
- IEEE 802.3bw (100BASE-T1)
- OPEN Alliance TC1 specification
- BroadR-Reach specification
- Automotive EMC compliance

## 约束
- Maximum cable length 15 meters
- 100 Mbps fixed data rate
- Single twisted pair only
- Master/slave configuration required
- Automotive temperature range compliance

## 推荐工具
- BroadR-Reach PHY transceiver
- MDIO interface for configuration
- TDR cable tester
